# KNOWN GAP — durable repro for the STAGING-MOVE class at the MATCH-ARM write
# site (`assign_match_arm_to_result`).
#
# The arm-assign moves the arm value into the match's owned result slot and
# emits its own `move_zero` on a source that is read again — the same
# `[Mv] _dst = copy _src; move_zero _src; … copy _src` shape as the slice cell,
# in a different costume. Benign TODAY only because the backend elides the
# zero, which Core #8 forbids treating as a pass.
#
# ⚠ The gap is the WRITE SITE, not this program's output: at HEAD this fixture
# builds clean and prints `ok`. The only instrument that can observe the defect
# is `GG_STAGING_MOVE_GUARD=fatal`, so the `#[ignore]`d test asserts the
# INTENDED state — zero `StagingMoveIntoOwnedSlot` violations under the
# promoter — which is RED at HEAD (`BUILD_RC=101`, 1 violation at
# `@eval_stmt_list bb7 i0`) by construction. Graduate it (un-ignore, delete
# this copy, drop the ledger row in `tests/gaps/STAGING_MOVE_BURNDOWN.txt`,
# lower the lint's TRIP_CEILING) the round the match-arm write site routes
# through `LoweringContext::assign_with_move_follow_through`.
#
# A copy of the live `tests/fixtures/snag31_match_arm_move_into_owned.gg`: the
# hand-minimised shapes tried do not reach the site.
#
# Regression pin for Snag #31: Tier 2a consume-site validator panicked
# on `Completion c = match … : case Ok(x): ^x …` shape — the user-opt-in
# `!arg` move from a match-bound pattern variable into a named owned
# local. The pattern IS sound per CLAUDE.md "Ownership at Consuming
# Positions" (`!arg` is the first move-eligible shape); the validator
# was over-eager because `assign_match_arm_to_result` didn't tag the
# match's result_local as Owned after the Move-mode arm-assign.
#
# Surfaced 2026-05-10 by gorget-js's eval_stmt_list / eval_try /
# eval_while / eval_for_c / eval_do_while / abstract_equals — every
# loop-body and try/catch in the JS interpreter uses this idiom.
#
# Fix: `assign_match_arm_to_result` now calls `ctx.set_owned(result_local)`
# after the Move-mode assign, completing the writer-side typed tagging
# so downstream Move-mode assigns from the result_local see Owned.

public enum Completion:
    Normal(String)
    Throw(String)

Result[Completion, String] eval_stmt(int x):
    if x > 0:
        return Ok(Completion.Normal("ok"))
    else:
        return Error("err")

Result[Completion, String] eval_stmt_list(Vector[int] stmts):
    Completion last = Completion.Normal("init")
    int i = 0
    while i < stmts.len():
        int s = stmts.get(i).unwrap()
        Completion c = match eval_stmt(s):
            case Ok(x):
                ^x    # Snag #31 trigger: ^move from match arm
            case Error(e):
                return Error(e)
        match c:
            case Completion.Normal(_):
                last = ^c
            else:
                return Ok(^c)
        i = i + 1
    return Ok(last)

void main():
    Vector[int] v = [1, 2, 3]
    Result[Completion, String] r = eval_stmt_list(v)
    match r:
        case Ok(c):
            print("ok")
        case Error(_):
            print("err")
